### Naming conventions

- **Dated content** (date IS part of identity): `YYYY-MM-DD Title.md` — meeting notes, event or conference notes, dated proposal versions, daily notes.
- **Everything else**: descriptive name, **no date prefix**. Sort via frontmatter `created:` and the vault's sort configuration rather than filenames.
- **Templates**: `[Type] Template.md` (e.g., `Methodology Note Template.md`).
- **People**: `Full Name.md`.
- **Clippings**: `Clean Title.md` — **no date prefix**. Capture the date in `published` (priority: `published` > content-inferred > URL path date > `created`) and sort/filter via frontmatter, not the filename. Clean titles: remove site names, author attribution, URL artefacts, ticker symbols. Exception: annual shareholder letters keep the year (e.g. `1999 Berkshire Hathaway Shareholder Letter.md`).

### Dates — YYYY-MM-DD everywhere

- Filenames, frontmatter, directory names — one format.
- ISO-8601 ordering means filesystem-collation matches chronological order.
- Avoid locale-specific date formats (no `MM/DD/YYYY`, no `5 May 2026`).

### Rating scale

- Ratings use the 7-point scale: `1` through `7`.
- Why 7: middle is `4`, leaves `2`/`3` and `5`/`6` for forced discrimination on either side. Five-point scales collapse to "good / OK / bad"; ten-point scales lose precision via false granularity.

### HTML in notes

- Obsidian renders inline HTML in reading view and live preview.
- **Inline `style=""` only** — `<style>` tags and CSS class-based styling are ignored. Put all styling in inline `style=""` attributes with hardcoded hex values.
- Obsidian's own CSS variables (`var(--text-normal)`, `var(--background-primary)`, etc.) work inside inline styles.
- SVG with inline styles also renders.
- CSS snippets in `.obsidian/snippets/` style Obsidian's UI chrome, not user HTML in notes.

